# Official Documentation
`docs/` is the official public documentation. `example/` remains playground/debug infrastructure.

Every STABLE public component must document:
- Overview
- When to use / when not to use
- Related components
- Complete demos
- Props / Events / Slots / Expose / Models / Public types
- Accessibility and keyboard behavior when interactive
- Design tokens when customizable
- Version/stability information

- API tables should be generated from source contracts/metadata.
- Do not hand-maintain partial API tables as source of truth.
- Running demo source and displayed copyable source must be the same file.
- Complex components require multiple scenario demos.
- Documentation must fail CI when it drifts from public API contracts.
